- discuss hologram basics and mixed reality.
## Artificial Neural Networks (ANN)
The human brain contains about **86 billion neurons** that pass signals to one another. An **Artificial Neural Network** imitates this idea in software. It has an **input layer** (receives data, e.g. the pixels of a picture), one or more **hidden layers** (process the data), and an **output layer** (gives the answer, e.g. “cat” or “dog”). Each connection has a **weight** (strength). During **training**, the network is shown many labelled examples and adjusts its weights whenever its answer is wrong, until it becomes accurate.
